<div class="panel"><h2>AI narrative (local, cited)</h2>
<ul class="story" data-ai-endpoint="/api/ai/narrative?key=MLC-3%20IMS%202026-06">
<li>MLC3_IMS_2026-06.mpp contains 250 activities (38 summary rollups excluded), statused to a data date of 06/05/2026 with 150 complete and 100 to go. [MLC-3 Flight Campaign (UID 1000, MLC3_IMS_2026-06.mpp)]</li>
<li>The computed finish is 12/21/2026 — 33 calendar days later than the 11/18/2026 finish computed from IMS 2026-04. [MLC-3 Launch (UID 9001, MLC3_IMS_2026-06.mpp)]</li>
<li>The controlling path runs through Lunar Cargo Module servicing and fairing encapsulation into vehicle stacking, integrated test, wet dress rehearsal and the launch-readiness reviews. [Vehicle — Integrated Vehicle Test (IVT) (UID 2222, MLC3_IMS_2026-06.mpp)]</li>
<li>Five activities on the fairing-encapsulation chain carry −4 working days of total float: the chain is already behind the launch window without recovery. [LCM — Payload Fairing Encapsulation (UID 2158, MLC3_IMS_2026-06.mpp)]</li>
<li>Six of the 16 DCMA-14 checks fail: Logic (14%), High Float (29%), Negative Float (5%), Missed Activities (13.7%), CPLI (0.91) and BEI (0.87). [MLC-3 Flight Campaign (UID 1000, MLC3_IMS_2026-06.mpp)]</li>
<li>Baseline throughput is the leading indicator: BEI 0.87 means work is completing 13% slower than baselined, concentrated in the Stage 2 avionics retest chain (+12 wd finish variance). [Stage 2 — Avionics Functional Test (UID 2093, MLC3_IMS_2026-06.mpp)]</li>
<li>A single 5-working-day margin activity protects the launch window and it sits on the critical path — the program is spending its last buffer. [Schedule Margin — Pad Ops (UID 2247, MLC3_IMS_2026-06.mpp)]</li>
</ul></div>
<div class="panel" id="askPanel"><h2>Ask the AI</h2>
<p class="muted"><b>AI can err — verify against citations.</b> Ask anything about the loaded
data: with a local model active (Ollama) you get a full written analysis grounded in the
engine's computed, cited facts — the matching facts are always shown alongside. With no
local model active you get the cited facts themselves; <a href="/settings">enable Ollama in AI
Settings</a> for interpretation.</p>
<p class="muted"><b>Figure check is role-aware.</b> In <i>strict</i> and <i>annotate</i> modes a number
the model writes is matched against the figures in the cited facts, and a digit that appears only in
an activity <i>name</i> or <i>ID</i> (e.g. "Milestone 2099", UID&nbsp;6077) — never as an engine
value — is treated as an identifier the model has re-used in another role (a finish year, a
count): <i>strict</i> discards that answer and <i>annotate</i> flags it — and the identifier
check runs <i>before</i> the derived-figure check, so a re-used ID can never pass as a coincidental
derivation. Writing an ID <i>as</i> an ID ("UID&nbsp;143", a quoted activity name) is fine; dates
count as whole dates, not digit fragments; a derived whole number must reconstruct exactly; and a
figure re-written with a <i>different explicit unit</i> than the engine stated (a "5%" re-used as
"5&nbsp;days") is likewise discarded/flagged. A digit
that is also a genuine value is untouched (collision-safe). <i>Interpretive</i> mode is not
figure-gated at all. Read any figure against the cited facts — the meaning, not just the
number.</p>
<div class="viz-controls">
<label>About <select id="askScope"><option value="">Workbook — all 3 versions</option><option value="MLC-3 IMS 2026-04">MLC-3 IMS 2026-04</option><option value="MLC-3 IMS 2026-05">MLC-3 IMS 2026-05</option><option value="MLC-3 IMS 2026-06" selected>MLC-3 IMS 2026-06</option></select></label>
<input id="askInput" type="text" size="60" maxlength="500" placeholder="e.g. Why is the finish slipping? How many critical activities?">
<button id="askBtn" type="button">Ask</button></div>
<div class="viz-controls"><span class="muted">Driving path (exact, no AI):</span>
<label>to UID <input id="drivePathUid" type="number" min="1" step="1" style="width:7em" placeholder="UID"></label>
<button id="drivePathBtn" type="button">Show driving path</button></div>
<div id="askOut"></div></div>
</main>
<div class="cui-banner cui bottom" data-no-i18n>Controlled Unclassified Information • CUI</div>
</div>
</x-dc>
<script type="text/x-dc" data-dc-script>
class Component extends DCLogic {
  componentDidMount() {
    window.SF_PAGE_MAP = Object.assign(window.SF_PAGE_MAP || {}, {
      "/": "Recreation — Dashboard.dc.html",
      "/analysis/MLC-3%20IMS%202026-06": "Recreation — Analysis.dc.html",
      "/analysis/MLC-3%20IMS%202026-05": "Recreation — Analysis.dc.html",
      "/analysis/MLC-3%20IMS%202026-04": "Recreation — Analysis.dc.html",
    });
    var probe = new URLSearchParams(location.search).get("boot");
    var scripts = [
      "theme.js", "checklist.js", "gantt.js", "timescale.js", "colresize.js", "a11y.js",
      "translate.js", "app.js", "scatter.js", "histogram.js", "ai_polish.js", "ask.js",
      "heartbeat.js", "chartframe.js", "target.js", "globe.js", "sysmon.js", "hints.js",
      "vizhints.js",
    ];
    if (probe) scripts = scripts.slice(0, Number(probe));
    console.log("SFBoot starting", scripts.length, "scripts");
    window.SFBoot(scripts, function () { console.log("SFBoot done"); });
  }
  renderVals() {
    return {};
  }
}
</script>
</body>
</html>
